course: dictionary
lesson: 10405
title: Tricksters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trickster is a person who tricks or cheats people, often to get their money. «The internet also has tricksters.» Some people online pretend to be someone else so they can fool you, so the word helps you spot that danger.
explain: In myths and folk tales, a trickster is a clever, playful character who plays tricks on others. Anansi the spider, Coyote and Loki are famous examples. In «In Zootopia, Nick Wilde the fox is a sly trickster», sly means clever in a sneaky way.
explain: Tricksters often pull at your feelings. «Tricksters use stories that pull at a kind child's heart.» They may try to make you hurry or keep secrets. «Real people are happy to wait for your grown-up; tricksters get annoyed and leave.» So if someone pushes you to rush, stop, check, and tell a grown-up.
fact: A trickster is a person who tricks or cheats people, often to get their money.
fact: In myths and folk tales, a trickster is a clever, playful character, such as Anansi the spider, Coyote or Loki.
fact: «Tricksters use stories that pull at a kind child's heart.»
fact: A real person who is safe will wait for your grown-up to check things.
fact: Related words: con artist, cheat and fraudster all mean someone who deceives people.
exercise: «The internet also has tricksters.» What is a trickster? | A kind teacher who helps you with maths | A type of tree found in forests | *A person who tricks or cheats people
exercise: In myths, Anansi the spider is a trickster. What kind of character is a trickster in a myth? | *A clever, playful character who plays tricks | A serious king who always tells the truth | A tired farmer who sleeps all day
exercise: «Real people are happy to wait for your grown-up; tricksters get annoyed and leave.» What does this tell you about a trickster? | They like to be asked lots of questions | They are always patient and calm | They wait for your grown-up to arrive | *They get annoyed and leave when you wait
test: Which word is closest in meaning to trickster? | Gardener | Sunshine | Pencil | *Fraudster
test: «In Zootopia, Nick Wilde the fox is a sly trickster.» What does sly mean here? | *Clever in a sneaky way | Lost and afraid | Kind and gentle | Very loud and noisy
exam: Ruby gets a message from a stranger pretending to be her cousin and asking for money. What word fits this person? | *Trickster | Lifeguard | Librarian | Teacher
